   ("The headliner is the part that gets skipped",
    ["Headliners are the most under-cleaned surface in any vehicle, and on a camping vehicle they are frequently the most contaminated.",
     "Smoke rises, and campfire smoke that came in on clothing and gear settles upward into the headliner fabric where it sits. It is also where the smell lives. Cleaning the seats and the carpet of a smoky vehicle without touching the headliner leaves the largest reservoir of the smell exactly where it was.",
     "Headliners have to be cleaned carefully \u2014 too much moisture and the adhesive under the fabric lets go \u2014 but they can be cleaned, and on a Kewaskum vehicle after a season of weekends it makes the largest difference of any single surface."]),
